> Preserve original recordings, shifts, warmup and fixed endpoint

The [FSDD v1.0.10 source](https://github.com/Jakobovski/free-spoken-digit-dataset/tree/v1.0.10)
is retained with its CC BY-SA4.0 attribution and release provenance. The pinned
release ZIP has16419872 bytes and SHA256
c680098f5d2355ba7cc4bd8b0ca9e0a24c00ebe3b4c552208889a4d28d4fbc2b.
There are27 original mono8kHz PCM16 clips, digits0/1/2. Takes0/1 are retained
for george, jackson and yweweler; take0 for lucas, nicolas and theo. Use the first
1025 actual samples of each clip, with no resampling, peak normalization or
synthetic replacement. Four256-input/next-target windows start at0,256,512,768.
No window crosses a recording boundary; windows of one clip remain dependent.

Fit uses18 clips/four speakers and72 windows, validation3 theo clips/12 windows,
test6 yweweler clips/24 windows. Recording and speaker sets are disjoint across
these pools. This is a custom tiny teaching split, not the official FSDD test
protocol or72 independent speakers. Three prompts are the first384 codes of
held-out test recordings:128 observed codes and256 reference continuation
codes. They share source recordings with the test pool, never the fit pool.
Native audio preparation and LoadWaveStack retain/validate source, speaker and
start metadata. The report acquires missing inputs through the canonical native
preparation path; existing verified inputs are reused.

Input code at index t targets code t+1. Training NLL excludes positions0..31
and scores positions32..255,224 per window. Always pass start32 explicitly;
the older foundation stack's default127 is a different protocol. Three epochs
use Adam.001, batch8 and BatchOrder(72,8,8713):27 total updates, no checkpoint
selection, schedule, clipping, tuning or refit. All weights, first/final partials
and every gradient/update/iteration record remain available. A new store loads
the fixed third-epoch checkpoint exactly. No TF initial arrays were present;
this is the source native seed541 run, not a recorded TF trajectory comparison.

The complete program retains both synthesis loops. Cold start uses one code128
for each of two rows and2048 sampled codes per row, seed8729. Continuation uses
three observed128-code prompts and512 sampled codes, seed8731. The midpoint
MT19937 bank is drawn case first and then time, with u=(raw+.5)/2^32. Each step
selects one code by the inverse softmax CDF, feeds the sampled code back, and
retains its raw cached logits. No lower prompt truth enters generation. The
full native RF33 forward is checked at the first65 draws, every128th draw and
the final draw:369 probes across both runs, max error2.98e−8, tolerance2e−5.

Training uses native Float32 WaveNll. For original17-digit history summaries,
per-point max/logsumexp/target arithmetic is native Double, followed by a serial
row/time sum in the source order. A differently grouped whole-array reduction
changes only a few final bits; it must not silently replace that formatting
protocol. This summary choice does not alter the fitted Float32 gradients.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <random>
#include <numeric>
namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;
using T=n::Tensor;using A=std::map<std::string,T>;namespace fs=std::filesystem;
void Save(const fs::path& file,const A& fields){
 n::NamedTensors named;for(const auto& [key,value]:fields)named.emplace_back(key,value);
 n::save_npz(file.string(),named);
}
A Weights(const n::ParameterStore& p){
 A out;for(const auto& name:p.names())out.emplace(name,p.at(name).detach().clone());return out;
}
bool Equal(const A& a,const A& b){
 if(a.size()!=b.size())return false;
 for(const auto& [key,value]:a)if(!b.count(key)||!n::equal_bits(value,b.at(key)))return false;
 return true;
}
A Partials(const n::ParameterStore& p,const std::vector<T>& g){
 A out;for(std::size_t k=0;k<g.size();++k)out.emplace(p.names()[k],g[k].detach());return out;
}


const m::WaveStackConfig config{4,8,5,1,256};
T Predict(n::ParameterStore& p,const T& codes){
 n::NoGradGuard guard;return m::WaveStack(p,n::one_hot(codes,256),config).logits.detach().contiguous();
}
double SerialMean(const T& points){auto values=points.to_vector<double>();return std::accumulate(values.begin(),values.end(),0.)/values.size();}
double Nll(const T& logits,const m::WaveData& data){
 n::NoGradGuard guard;auto z=n::cast(n::slice_axis(logits,1,32,256),n::DType::Float64);
 auto y=n::slice_axis(data.target,1,32,256),maximum=n::max(z,{2},true);
 auto mass=n::sum(n::exp(z-maximum),{2});auto actual=n::sum(z*n::one_hot(y,256,1,0,n::DType::Float64),{2});
 return SerialMean(n::squeeze(maximum,{2})+n::log(mass)-actual);
}
struct Draw {A fields;double parity=0;std::vector<double> errors;std::vector<std::int32_t> times,rows;};
Draw Sample(n::ParameterStore& p,const T& prefix,int count,std::uint32_t seed){
 n::NoGradGuard guard;const int cases=int(prefix.size(0)),warm=int(prefix.size(1)),width=warm+count;
 std::mt19937 rng(seed);std::vector<double> values(static_cast<std::size_t>(cases*count));
 for(auto& u:values)u=(double(rng())+.5)/4294967296.;
 auto bank=n::from_vector(values,{cases,count});
 std::vector<T> code_rows,head_rows;Draw out;
 for(int row=0;row<cases;++row){
  m::WaveStackCache cache(p,config);std::vector<std::int32_t> codes;
  auto observed=n::select(prefix,0,row).to_vector<std::int32_t>();T scores;
  for(auto code:observed){codes.push_back(code);scores=cache.next(code);}
  std::vector<T> heads;
  for(int step=0;step<count;++step){
   heads.push_back(scores);
   if(step<65||step%128==0||step+1==count){
    const int end=warm+step,start=std::max(0,end-m::WaveStackField(config));
    std::vector<std::int32_t> context(codes.begin()+start,codes.begin()+end);
    auto native=Predict(p,n::from_vector(context,{1,end-start}));
    auto last=n::reshape(n::select(native,1,native.size(1)-1),{256});
    double error=n::max(n::abs(n::cast(scores,n::DType::Float64)-n::cast(last,n::DType::Float64))).item();
    out.parity=std::max(out.parity,error);out.errors.push_back(error);out.times.push_back(step);out.rows.push_back(row);
   }
   auto z=n::cast(scores,n::DType::Float64);auto mass=n::exp(z-n::max(z));
   auto cumulative=n::cumsum(mass/n::sum(mass),0);
   double u=values[static_cast<std::size_t>(row*count+step)];
   int code=int(n::sum(n::cast(n::less_equal(cumulative,u),n::DType::Int32)).item());code=std::min(code,255);
   codes.push_back(code);scores=cache.next(code);
  }
  if(cache.consumed()!=width)throw std::runtime_error("Cache consumes all observed and sampled codes");
  code_rows.push_back(n::from_vector(codes,{width}));head_rows.push_back(n::stack(heads));
 }
 if(out.parity>=2e-5)throw std::runtime_error("Cached/native RF33 parity");
 out.fields={{"codes",n::stack(code_rows)},{"logits",n::stack(head_rows)},{"uniform",bank}};return out;
}
void WriteAudio(const fs::path& root,const std::string& name,const T& codes){
 for(std::int64_t row=0;row<codes.size(0);++row)
  n::write_wav((root/(name+"_"+std::to_string(row)+".wav")).string(),n::reshape(n::mu_law_decode(n::select(codes,0,row)),{codes.size(1),1}),8000);
}
int main(){
 const fs::path root="build/wavenet";fs::create_directories(root/"phases");n::set_num_threads(4);
 fs::path inputs=fs::path(dm::datasets::data_home())/"wavenet";
 if(const auto* path=std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_WAVENET_DIR"))inputs=path;
 if(!fs::exists(inputs/"wavenet_stack.npz"))dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("audio",inputs.string());
 const auto data=m::LoadWaveStack(inputs);const auto& fit=data.pools[0];const auto& validation=data.pools[1];const auto& test=data.pools[2];
 fs::copy_file(inputs/"wavenet_stack.npz",root/"data.npz",fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
 fs::copy_file(inputs/"manifest.json",root/"data_manifest.json",fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
 n::ParameterStore p(541);{n::NoGradGuard guard;m::WaveStack(p,n::one_hot(n::zeros({1,2},n::DType::Int32),256),config);}
 if(p.count()!=5068||p.size()!=34||m::WaveStackField(config)!=33)throw std::runtime_error("5068/34/RF33 source census");
 Save(root/"initial_arrays.npz",Weights(p));Save(root/"initial_outputs.npz",{{"logits",Predict(p,test.input)}});
 n::Optimizer optimizer(p,.001,{n::OptimizerKind::Adam});n::BatchOrder order(72,8,8713);
 std::ofstream history(root/"history.tsv"),batches(root/"batches.tsv");history.precision(17);
 history<<"epoch\tvalidation_nll\tvalidation_bits_per_sample\n";batches<<"epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
 auto source_ids=fit.source.to_vector<std::int32_t>();int updates=0;m::WaveData first;std::vector<double> validation_bits;
 for(int epoch=1;epoch<=3;++epoch){
  order.begin_epoch();for(;;){auto rows=order.next();if(rows.empty())break;auto batch=m::WaveRows(fit,rows);
   if(!updates){first=batch;Save(root/"first_batch.npz",{{"input",batch.input},{"target",batch.target}});
    Save(root/"first_forward.npz",{{"logits",Predict(p,batch.input)}});}
   auto logits=m::WaveStack(p,n::one_hot(batch.input,256),config).logits;
   auto loss=m::WaveNll(logits,batch.target,256,32);auto gradients=n::grad(loss,p.parameters());
   auto phase=root/"phases"/("batch"+std::to_string(updates));Save(phase.string()+"-gradient.npz",Partials(p,gradients));
   if(!updates)Save(root/"initial_gradients.npz",Partials(p,gradients));
   optimizer.step(gradients);auto after=Weights(p);Save(phase.string()+"-after.npz",after);
   Save(phase.string()+"-iterations.npz",{{"iterations",n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{optimizer.iterations()},{1})}});
   if(!updates)Save(root/"first_after.npz",after);
   for(auto row:rows)batches<<epoch<<'\t'<<updates<<'\t'<<row<<'\t'<<source_ids[row]<<'\n';++updates;
  }
  auto prediction=Predict(p,validation.input);double loss=Nll(prediction,validation);
  if(std::abs(m::WaveNll(prediction,validation.target,256,32).item()-loss)>2e-5)throw std::runtime_error("Float32 graph and Double scalar loss");
  history<<epoch<<'\t'<<loss<<'\t'<<loss/std::log(2.)<<'\n';validation_bits.push_back(loss/std::log(2.));
  Save(root/("epoch"+std::to_string(epoch)+"_arrays.npz"),Weights(p));
  Save(root/("epoch"+std::to_string(epoch)+"_validation.npz"),{{"logits",prediction}});
 }
 if(updates!=27||optimizer.iterations()!=27)throw std::runtime_error("27 Adam writes");
 p.save((root/"final.npz").string());Save(root/"model_arrays.npz",Weights(p));
 auto final_logits=m::WaveStack(p,n::one_hot(first.input,256),config).logits;
 Save(root/"final_gradients.npz",Partials(p,n::grad(m::WaveNll(final_logits,first.target,256,32),p.parameters())));
 n::ParameterStore restored(541);{n::NoGradGuard guard;m::WaveStack(restored,n::one_hot(n::zeros({1,2},n::DType::Int32),256),config);}
 restored.load((root/"final.npz").string(),true);if(!Equal(Weights(p),Weights(restored)))throw std::runtime_error("Fresh exact restore");
 auto before=Weights(restored);auto logits=Predict(restored,test.input);Save(root/"outputs.npz",{{"logits",logits}});
 if(!n::equal_bits(logits,Predict(restored,test.input)))throw std::runtime_error("Frozen repeat logits");
 auto shifted=test.input+71;shifted=n::where(n::greater_equal(shifted,256),shifted-256,shifted);
 auto changed=n::where(n::greater_equal(n::reshape(n::arange(0,256),{1,256}),128),shifted,test.input);
 auto altered=Predict(restored,changed);Save(root/"future_control.npz",{{"input",changed},{"logits",altered}});
 if(n::max(n::abs(n::slice_axis(logits-altered,1,0,128))).item()!=0)throw std::runtime_error("Future-token prefix invariance");
 auto encoded=n::one_hot(n::slice_axis(n::take_rows(test.input,{0}),1,0,64),256).requires_grad_();
 auto causal=m::WaveStack(restored,encoded,config).logits;
 auto objective=n::sum(n::slice_axis(n::slice_axis(causal,1,48,49),2,0,1));auto gradient=n::grad(objective,{encoded})[0];
 if(n::max(n::abs(n::slice_axis(gradient,1,0,16))).item()!=0||n::max(n::abs(n::slice_axis(gradient,1,49,64))).item()!=0||
    n::sum(n::abs(n::slice_axis(gradient,1,16,49))).item()<=1e-6)throw std::runtime_error("Exact RF33 derivative support");
 Save(root/"causality.npz",{{"encoded_input",encoded.detach()},{"logits",causal.detach()},{"gradient",gradient.detach()}});
 auto codes=n::cast(n::arange(0,256),n::DType::Int32);
 if(!n::equal_bits(n::mu_law_encode(n::mu_law_decode(codes,256,n::DType::Float64)),codes))throw std::runtime_error("All256 codec bins roundtrip");
 auto cold=Sample(restored,n::full({2,1},128,n::DType::Int32),2048,8729);
 Save(root/"unconditional.npz",cold.fields);WriteAudio(root,"unconditional",cold.fields.at("codes"));
 auto again=Sample(restored,n::full({2,1},128,n::DType::Int32),2048,8729);
 if(!Equal(cold.fields,again.fields))throw std::runtime_error("Repeated full cold-start draws");
 auto prompt=n::slice_axis(data.prompts,1,0,128).contiguous();auto continuation=Sample(restored,prompt,512,8731);
 continuation.fields["source_ids"]=data.prompt_source_ids;
 Save(root/"continuation.npz",continuation.fields);WriteAudio(root,"continuation",continuation.fields.at("codes"));WriteAudio(root,"reference",data.prompts);
 if(!n::equal_bits(prompt,n::slice_axis(continuation.fields.at("codes"),1,0,128)))throw std::runtime_error("Observed prompt preservation");
 if(!Equal(before,Weights(restored)))throw std::runtime_error("Inference modified store");
 {n::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto counts=m::WaveCountTargets(fit,32);auto unigram=counts.first/n::sum(counts.first),transition=counts.second/n::sum(counts.second,{1},true);
  Save(root/"baseline.npz",{{"unigram_probability",unigram},{"transition_probability",transition}});
  auto x=n::slice_axis(test.input,1,32,256),y=n::slice_axis(test.target,1,32,256);
  double unigram_nll=SerialMean(-n::log(n::gather(unigram,y))),transition_nll=SerialMean(-n::log(n::gather(n::reshape(transition,{65536}),x*256+y)));
  double loss=Nll(logits,test);std::vector<double> errors=cold.errors;errors.insert(errors.end(),continuation.errors.begin(),continuation.errors.end());
  std::vector<std::int32_t> times=cold.times,rows=cold.rows,kind(cold.errors.size(),0);
  times.insert(times.end(),continuation.times.begin(),continuation.times.end());rows.insert(rows.end(),continuation.rows.begin(),continuation.rows.end());kind.insert(kind.end(),continuation.errors.size(),1);
  const auto probes=std::int64_t(errors.size());if(probes!=369)throw std::runtime_error("All369 full RF probe heads");
  Save(root/"cache_probes.npz",{{"error",n::from_vector(errors,{probes})},{"time",n::from_vector(times,{probes})},{"row",n::from_vector(rows,{probes})},{"kind",n::from_vector(kind,{probes})}});
  Save(root/"summary.npz",{{"validation_bits",n::from_vector(validation_bits,{3})},{"test_bits",n::full({},loss/std::log(2.),n::DType::Float64)},
   {"unigram_bits",n::full({},unigram_nll/std::log(2.),n::DType::Float64)},{"transition_bits",n::full({},transition_nll/std::log(2.),n::DType::Float64)}});
  std::print("| Fixed source protocol | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Fit / validation / test windows |72 /12 /24|\n| Learned values / leaves |5068 /34|\n| Receptive field / warmup |33 /32|\n| Adam writes / generated codes |27 /5632|\n| Cache/native full-head probes |369|\n| Max probe error |{:.3g}|\n| Test bits per mu-law sample |{:.6f}|\n| Fit-only unigram bits |{:.6f}|\n| Fit-only transition bits |{:.6f}|\n| Uniform bits |8|\n",std::max(cold.parity,continuation.parity),loss/std::log(2.),unigram_nll/std::log(2.),transition_nll/std::log(2.));
 }
}
