> Keep the negative likelihood result and both baselines visible

Fitting-only Laplace1 counts estimate a256-code unigram and a256×256 transition
row for each preceding code. Counts use only scored fitting positions32..255;
validation/test observations do not fit the baseline. Transition uses the true
preceding code when scoring test windows, just as the neural model is teacher
forced. It does not receive a free-running reference future. Uniform codes
cost exactly8 bits per sample. The fixed neural endpoint improves only slightly
on uniform and remains worse than both fitted baselines.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wv_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
