> Audit evidence and interpretation

The complete report reproduces22 original NPZ archives/9283192 values and81
captured gradient/update/iteration archives/273699 values exactly, together with
batch/history TSVs, the source manifest and all eight WAVs. Numerical plots are
new native figures; they retain every stated time point rather than reproducing
the old raster drawing style. Programs and native model/cache calls remain
editable here. Restored likelihood, derivatives, probes and generation leave
the store unchanged. The cached snapshot owns its required Float32 weights and
histories; invalid steps preserve state, reset restores true beginning and
clone forks an independent stream. Python uses next; R uses next_code because
next is reserved R syntax. Gate vectors return copied owning Tensor handles.

`scripts/check_generative_wavenet.py` independently verifies27675 original PCM
samples,55296 shifted input/target code values,1152 prompt codes,7618560 forward
values,163356 partials,34 finite differences,27 exact Adam writes and16384
structural derivatives. All5632 generation heads come from independent RF33
context evaluation, not a second implementation of the circular cache. All
sampled codes, midpoint MT banks and7170 exported PCM16 values match exactly.
Maximum forward/partial/sampling-head differences are2.55e−8/7.61e−9/3.06e−8.
Initial zero post biases can land on ReLU boundaries; finite differences use
fitted smooth coordinates while initial VJPs use the source derivative-zero rule.

Nine new cache tests plus527 selected C++ tests,281 Python tests and2119 R
expectations in56 files pass. All14 new definitions, six compiled header examples,
six clangd hovers and checkout/installed standalone headers pass. Report/export
checks also retain audio assets and rerun a report when a referenced WAV is
missing. The original native run and phase pins live in
`build/nn-report-conversion/wavenet/baseline.json`; numerical/cache/binding evidence
is under `wavenet_core/`. The source negative result is retained: this tiny fixed
endpoint is worse than both fitting-only baselines and supports no benchmark
speech, vocoder or recognition claim.

